ual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +18% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -223% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 67% confirm genuine pricing power.","The company is burning through $36M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -15.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 0.2% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 7.2% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-1.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 91% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.0032362459546931175},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (87% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.133},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 53/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Healthcare peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimb